ed": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`Table.transform` and `Table.transform_sql` now take `strict`, and `sqlite-utils transform` has a `--strict/--no-strict` option that passes it through. The check passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_transform.py tests/test_cli.py` gives 270 passed, 3 skipped. The skips are the `Requires compiled ext.c` tests, unrelated to this change.\n\nI read the diff of `sqlite_utils/db.py` and `sqlite_utils/cli.py` against the spec, and it matches. I did not read the doc changes in `docs/python-api.rst` and `docs/cli.rst`; I only have the implementer's report that they were added.\n\nThe spec asked whether the existing transaction handling already rolls back a failed strict conversion. The implementer says it does, because the work runs inside `self.db.atomic()`, so I left it unchanged. The tests I ran pass, but I didn't confirm that any of them covers a row that fails strict validation.\n\nNothing is committed.", "ttft_ms": 1751, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 6607, "uuid": "029e890e-4195-4501-ba96-87bcd29c5f9e", "ttft_stream_ms": 1217, "time_to_request_ms": 18, "first_content_frame_ms": 1217, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
